### 2. MATHEMATICAL & ACADEMIC SPECIFICATION ONLY
This repository is a scientific and engineering publication. Its subject
matter is the study and implementation of public algorithms: finite-field
(Galois) arithmetic, attractor maps built on the Chinese Remainder Theorem,
a deterministic gas model inspired by the Landauer principle, XMSS
post-quantum signatures, and distributed consensus machinery.

Nothing in this repository is a financial product, a financial service, an
investment offering, an exchange, a transfer agent, or a custody service.
The authors do not operate the network, do not hold, control, or transmit
value on behalf of anyone, and do not solicit users. Compiling, running, or
studying this code creates no contractual or other relationship with the
authors. Any economic significance a third party assigns to tokens created
by the network is that third party's own doing, outside this publication.

